    "updated_at": "2022-07-07T21:03:57Z",
    "body": "From a web compatibility standpoint I think that throwing an exception upon use of `imageOrientation: none` is too aggressive - it would cause web pages to completely stop working, rather than potentially (not definitely) displaying incorrect results. A deprecation warning to the console would be more developer- and user-friendly.\r\n\r\nAgree with trying to minimize the deprecation and switch-over period.\r\n\r\nCC @mrdoob since the main use of this dictionary element is Three.js.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
