    "updated_at": "2024-07-02T23:41:05Z",
    "body": "Multiple browser vendors discussed this a while back and (99% sure, from recollection) agreed to change `createImageBitmap`'s behavior. The HTML spec should be updated to say: first EXIF orientation is applied, and then if `imageOrientation` is `flipY`, the image is flipped vertically. CC @kdashg @kkinnunen-apple @lexaknyazev @RafaelCintron\r\n\r\nThis behavior is tested in the WebGL conformance suite: https://github.com/KhronosGroup/WebGL/blob/main/sdk/tests/conformance/textures/misc/exif-orientation.html , [runnable online here](https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/sdk/tests/conformance/textures/misc/exif-orientation.html?webglVersion=2&quiet=0&quick=1).",
